diff --git a/docs/reference/rewriter.md b/docs/reference/rewriter.md
index e6c7ebda..8b96e716 100644
--- a/docs/reference/rewriter.md
+++ b/docs/reference/rewriter.md
@@ -67,9 +67,9 @@ To enroll a cut for any game's own module:
 ### Index copied before the bounds check
 
 - **Symptom:** `jump table <addr>` assertion where the index is a copy made before the check (`mov w0,w18`, then 41 instructions holding two other jump tables on `x0`, then `cmp w18,#4; b.hi; ldrsw x18,[x11,x0,lsl #2]; add x18,x18,x11; br x18`).
-- **Cause:** every other form follows copies made after the bounds check.
-- **Fix:** `check_before_copy` accepts the `cmp` and `b.hi` right before the load when a `mov wI, wS` is the last writer of both registers; capstone lists a `cmp`'s first operand as written, which the search skips. The search follows the function boundary rather than an arbitrary instruction count, stopping at undecodable gaps and calls that can clobber either register. It runs only when every other form has failed.
-- **Found on:** [DRAGON QUEST XI S: Echoes of an Elusive Age – Definitive Edition](../../dm/games/01006C300E9F0000/README.md) `main+0x2dd8cd0`; [Mario + Rabbids Kingdom Battle](../../dm/games/010067300059A000/README.md) `subsdk0+0x7340b8`, whose copy is 71 instructions before the load, across two switches preserving both registers (beyond the former 64-instruction limit).
+- **Cause:** every other form follows copies made after the bounds check. A nearer `cmp` of the same register can also hide that check: the walk follows the copy back to the source, meets a reload of the source, and rejects the site because the index changed, without looking at the `cmp` / `b.hi` directly in front of the load.
+- **Fix:** `check_before_copy` accepts the `cmp` and `b.hi` right before the load when a `mov wI, wS` is the last writer of both registers; capstone lists a `cmp`'s first operand as written, which the search skips. The search follows the function boundary rather than an arbitrary instruction count, stopping at undecodable gaps and calls that can clobber either register. On the last attempt only, a compare the walk already reached is dropped when the index changed after it, so this check can run. It runs only when every other form has failed.
+- **Found on:** [DRAGON QUEST XI S: Echoes of an Elusive Age – Definitive Edition](../../dm/games/01006C300E9F0000/README.md) `main+0x2dd8cd0`; [Mario + Rabbids Kingdom Battle](../../dm/games/010067300059A000/README.md) `subsdk0+0x7340b8`, whose copy is 71 instructions before the load, across two switches preserving both registers (beyond the former 64-instruction limit); 無双OROCHI２ Ultimate (`0100153006300000`) `main+0x1bb31c`, where `ldr w18` sits between an earlier `cmp w18,#3` and `mov w0,w18; cmp w18,#3; b.hi`.
 - **Note:** before fixing one site, a census of all of them saves a run per site: a copy of `patch_nso.py` whose assert prints and continues found this one alone among the 25,508 `x18` sites. That `main` has no unwind entries for its first 70 MB, so the rewriter disassembles them as one function and takes 6 minutes (see [Long functions analysed in pieces](#long-functions-analysed-in-pieces)).
 
